# Amendment 1.0.3: adopt bounded flat-layout prerequisites under U10

The existing U10 requires an actual Rust layout worker and a qualified measurement → layout → routing user workflow. Legacy F16 [PR #29](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/29), at `6c198db81434ad4b1f318a6895fee8933a331d53`, is a proposed standalone flat-graph algorithm. It is not an ELK translation and has no native-runtime parity result. Its 529 newline-terminated production lines plus 572 test lines exceed the ordinary production and authored review caps. This amendment assigns two meaningful prerequisites before implementation; it does not make the legacy draft an accepted feature.

The donor production SHA-256 is `fd713fada8d59d9654783236d64709ef47329afc7029f8c06b65131c9615f1ad`. The original `tests/layout.rs` is 572 lines with 15 test functions, SHA-256 `e7700f18f4f673e9a21fd7d1379234bc1014211f7722f48c456c91980ba5fe2a`. Historical descriptions of 530 source lines used a different counting convention; actual donor bytes contain 529 newline-terminated lines. The machine policy retains every original test name and these source identities.

## U10a: admit a canonical flat graph

U10a owns `syson-layout/src/types.rs`, `src/admission.rs`, `tests/admission.rs` and its evidence directory. It preserves the borrowed node/edge/options/limits and typed error contracts. Admission validates finite nonnegative dimensions/spacing, stable unique IDs, endpoint membership, count/ID/work/logical-workspace limits and the explicit unsupported container/port/pin branches. It prepares canonical node/edge order and forward/reverse adjacency through fallible buffers. Input data remains borrowed and unchanged.

The admitted graph carries original input references, canonical indices, maximum ID width, accumulated charged work and the logical workspace estimate. U10b consumes that result once; it must not reset the budget, repeat graph copying/sorting or bypass cancellation. Public API tests exercise actual admission, exact and +1 boundaries, malformed/unsupported inputs, permutations and early/interior/late cancellation. The known precharged n² ID sorts remain a bounded policy to measure, not a claim of optimal throughput or a CPU deadline.

The source estimate is 254 retained donor lines plus 35–55 factoring lines: at most 309 changed production lines. An upper planning estimate of 650 authored lines allows focused admission tests and coordinator wiring. These estimates are not executed or formatted Git counts. Count actual additions and deletions, including root wiring and authored documentation, before admitting execution.

## U10b: place the admitted graph

U10b follows landed U10a and owns `src/placement.rs`, the unchanged original `tests/layout.rs` and its evidence directory. It additively implements canonical SCC condensation, longest-path ranks, weak-component bands, checked coordinate arithmetic and edge classification. The public `layout`/result contract preserves original IDs/sizes, Right/Down directions, cycles, self-loops, parallel edges, disconnected graphs and zero-size/gap behavior. Cancellation or failure returns no partial layout.

All 15 original tests remain byte-for-byte, including the 512 three-node directed graphs in both directions. Those 1,024 checks establish the named invariants; they are not 1,024 native comparisons. The original error, work/memory/ID budget, cancellation, overflow/precision and trailing-gap cases remain required. The final composition also runs U10a admission tests and explicitly reviews any charge or cancellation-order change caused by factoring.

The remaining source estimate is 275 donor lines plus up to 20 factoring/wiring lines: at most 295 changed production lines. Adding all 572 original test lines gives 867 before any additional root wiring, notices, documentation or new tests. The conservative authored upper estimate is 890; the hard cap stays 900. If the formatted implementation would exceed either cap, adopt another meaningful SCC/rank child before coding. Do not delete tests, compress formatting, hide root wiring or infer a budget exception.

## Preserve the parent and actual callers

U10 retains every original source path, task, verification condition, U02/U09 dependency and owner hold. Its implementation additionally consumes U10b; its acceptance requires both U10a and U10b. The parent keeps the actual effective ELK/Sirius source/artifact/options and native invocation/comparison, worker lifecycle, typed result validation, fractional measurement provenance, document/revision/font/request affinity, staleness/cancellation, pins/ports/containers, routing/obstacles, history publication and supported-capacity obligations. U11's routing and interaction work remains separate.

The standalone kernel children can qualify their finite typed API independently of the unfinished UI. Both children remain std-only, with no runtime or build dependencies. The measurement interface is a source pin, not a crate dependency. Their source-preparation chain is U10a → U10b. This does not waive U02/U09 for parent implementation or turn borrowed f64 dimensions into a real measurement caller. The pinned main measurement interface is `syson-node-measurement/src/lib.rs` at `1f090ddc3f7c20797e5740ab1e7bcfa3895ab7c1`, SHA-256 `3006fc02a1d34827c435e427e62532e1cd3ec872d14158b6f57cc7b190eb218d`; actual conversion, stable identities and one numeric admission policy must be qualified through the real parent measurement → layout → routing path. No successful identity-layout fallback or Java/ELK production subprocess is introduced.

Native comparisons require the matching effective ELK/Sirius artifact and options, including cycles, self/parallel edges, disconnected graphs, fractional/long labels, both directions and required unsupported shapes. Compare declared geometry tolerances and readable outcomes; preserve raw differences and individually review intentional improvements. Synthetic graph invariants cannot replace the native source invocation, rendered obstacle clearance, crossing/path quality or user tasks.

Actual UI qualification remains required: 320/1440-pixel readability/clipping, selection and pan/zoom while computing, cancel/retry/stale results, worker disposal, focus and history, followed by the declared broader device/assistive-technology matrix. Native defects need not be copied, but an improvement needs its explicit compatibility and usability disposition. The parent and C99 remain OPEN while any required native, caller, worker, geometry, UI or capacity behavior is unsupported or unrun.

## Keep review and performance gates

Each child has a 400 changed handwritten production/900 authored line cap, counting additions plus deletions after ordinary formatting. Root alone owns `syson-layout/src/lib.rs`, Cargo manifest/lock, NOTICE and application registration. Source authors receive separate exclusive module/test leases only after amendment adoption and actual prerequisite admission; runtime execution remains serialized under coordinator ownership. This amendment grants no implementation or runtime lease and releases no existing held scope.

Use realistic IDs and graph shapes at 64/128/256/1024 nodes and representative edge densities. The separate 32-node/64-edge interactive workload remains a parent gate. Do not weaken numeric, work or allocation admission merely to hit a node count. Record two warmups and seven measured samples with all raw min/median/max; p95 needs at least 30 measured samples and a declared estimator. Keep logical work/estimated workspace, requested allocation traffic, peak live heap, process RSS, compute time and event-to-visible latency distinct. Preserve the existing workload-specific target ranges; no universal timing cutoff or capacity acceptance follows from this split.

The contract moves to `SYSON-RUST-COMPLETION/1.0.3`, with 782 review units: all prior 780 plus U10a/U10b. Every other obligation, source assignment, original test, prior evidence, 55 historical execution objects, integration history, RR08 split and named F10/F11 budget disposition remains. The unchanged original and normalized U10 fields are reconstructed and hashed by the policy; current source/brief bindings move to the new contract. Static refusal controls reject missing children, coherently removed dependency/readiness edges, broadened scopes/caps, detached parent acceptance and dropped original test/source/parent gates. These checks prove planning integrity only; independent runtime acceptance and RR16b/RR17 enforcement remain required.
